# CodeAlpha Stock Trading Platform

A console-based Java application developed as part of the **CodeAlpha Java Programming Internship – Task 2**.

## Features

- Display available stock market data
- Buy stocks
- Sell stocks
- Track stock holdings
- View transaction history
- View portfolio value
- Track portfolio performance
- Manage user balance
- Validate stock quantity and available balance

## Technologies Used

- Java 21
- Java Collections (`ArrayList`, `HashMap`)
- Object-Oriented Programming
- IntelliJ IDEA

## Project Structure

## How to Run

1. Open the project in IntelliJ IDEA.
2. Open `src/Main.java`.
3. Run the `Main` class.
4. Use the console menu to view market data, buy and sell stocks, and manage the portfolio.

## Task Requirements Covered

This project covers the main requirements of CodeAlpha Task 2:

- Simulating a basic stock trading environment
- Displaying market data
- Performing buy and sell operations
- Tracking portfolio holdings
- Managing stocks, users, and transactions using OOP
- Tracking portfolio performance
- Console-based implementation

